DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The uubbssaa driver provides support for the USB-to-RS232 Bridge chip used by
     a variety of serial adapters from Belkin and other vendors.

     Some 3G (UMTS/GPRS/GSM) cardbus(4) devices use a Belkin serial adapter
     and an ohci(4) controller to provide a common AT interface.

     The device is accessed through the ucom(4) driver which makes it behave
     like a tty(4).

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     The uubbssaa driver supports the following adapters:

           Axesstel MV100H
           Belkin F5U103
           Belkin F5U120
           e-Tek Labs Kwik232
           GoHubs GoCOM232
           Peracom single port serial adapter
           Qualcomm, Inc. ZTE AC8700
           Qualcomm, Inc. ZTE CDMA Technologies MSM

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     cardbus(4), tty(4), ucom(4), usb(4)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The uubbssaa driver first appeared in FreeBSD 5.0 and was ported to
     OpenBSD 3.3.

